  "body": "## What changed\n\n#631: the built-in Lathe (`lathe.mch`, X 0..320) refused **every thread**, with \"move 2 reaches -5.600 in X, the stroke is 0.000..320.000\".\n\n**Cause:** a thread pass is a chain of arcs **about the spindle axis**. Their far side, and the travel check's added quarter points, read negative X. That's the CL's antipode: the spindle turning the work, never a slide position. The machine check judged that raw signed X.\n\n**Fix** (`crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs`, the travel law in `check_ops`): on a machine of kind lathe, an XY arc **centred on the spindle axis** is judged in X by its **radius** at each extreme. Every other move keeps its signed X, so a real past-centre move is still judged against the band.\n\n**Not changed:** the band itself. `lathe_stroke::lathe_x_stays_a_centreline_band` records that a lathe's X is a one-sided centreline band. Whether a nose-radius face to centre (#630 / PR #640, which ends at X -r) should widen it is #640's call, not this PR's.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/631-lathe-spindle-arc-travel.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/lathe_thread_travel.rs`, 2/2:**\n  - `a_thread_passes_the_built_in_lathe`: **fails without the fix**, with the issue's exact message (\"move 2 reaches -5.600 in X…\").\n  - `a_real_over_travel_on_a_lathe_is_still_refused`: the same thread against an X stroke of 0..2 mm is refused \"… in X\".\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the app suites pass.\n- **Named:**\n\n  | Suite | Passed |\n  |---|---|\n  | machine | 32 |\n  | machine_library | 11 |\n  | turning_thread | 8 |\n  | lathe_post | 7 |\n  | lathe_post_g76 | 5 |\n  | lathe_post_refusals | 5 |\n  | tormach_machines | 5 |\n  | conformance | 6 |\n  | posting | 17 |\n  | setup_mounts_post | 5 |\n  | lathe_stroke | 5 |\n\n- **`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`:** clean, after the follow-up commit.\n- No golden changed. Fork synced at v0.16.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA Hub run on a lathe. The PathPilot lathe post is #626.\n\nChangelog: A thread no longer fails the built-in Lathe's machine check - an arc about the spindle axis is judged by its radius, not its far side's negative X (#631)\n\nFixes #631\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
